1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,710
A sleepover!

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:05,272
Sandy, you are invited to
a sleepover at the zoo!

3
00:00:16,995 --> 00:00:18,782
The Animated Zoo!

4
00:00:19,912 --> 00:00:21,922
Hello, I'm Milo!

5
00:00:21,962 --> 00:00:24,862
This is Sandy the baby
camel, and her Mama,

6
00:00:24,902 --> 00:00:26,523
in the sandy desert.

7
00:00:26,810 --> 00:00:28,020
A sleepover?

8
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:30,273
My very first night away from Mama!

9
00:00:30,568 --> 00:00:33,008
Mama camel nuzzles Sandy.

10
00:00:33,048 --> 00:00:34,778
Have fun, little one.

11
00:00:34,818 --> 00:00:37,148
I will be at the zoo gate in the morning.

12
00:00:37,477 --> 00:00:39,397
Where will Sandy sleep tonight?

13
00:00:39,437 --> 00:00:41,354
At the zoo, or at home?

14
00:00:44,684 --> 00:00:48,234
Sandy walks beside Mama, step, step, step,

15
00:00:48,274 --> 00:00:49,648
all the way to the zoo.

16
00:00:50,002 --> 00:00:53,212
A baby camel can walk beside its mama,

17
00:00:53,252 --> 00:00:55,585
when it is only half an hour old!

18
00:00:55,736 --> 00:00:57,986
Can a baby camel walk, soon after it is

19
00:00:58,026 --> 00:01:00,595
born? Yes, or no?

20
00:01:03,925 --> 00:01:07,295
At the zoo, Tumble the
baby elephant is waiting.

21
00:01:07,335 --> 00:01:09,335
Hooray, a sleepover!

22
00:01:09,542 --> 00:01:10,352
Hi, Sandy!

23
00:01:10,392 --> 00:01:12,522
We can play, and have supper, and sleep in

24
00:01:12,562 --> 00:01:13,710
the cozy barn!

25
00:01:14,081 --> 00:01:15,261
Bye-bye, Mama!

26
00:01:15,301 --> 00:01:16,522
See you in the morning!

27
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:18,960
They play hide and seek, and eat a yummy

28
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,522
supper. Munch, munch!

29
00:01:21,668 --> 00:01:25,428
Bedtime! In the cozy
barn, Tumble has a big,

30
00:01:25,468 --> 00:01:27,460
fluffy bed for Sandy.

31
00:01:27,607 --> 00:01:28,777
Wobble, wobble!

32
00:01:28,817 --> 00:01:30,557
Oh, this bed is too soft!

33
00:01:30,597 --> 00:01:32,460
I sink down, down, down!

34
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:36,080
Is the fluffy bed too soft, or too hard?

35
00:01:39,410 --> 00:01:41,890
At home, I kneel down on the warm sand,

36
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:43,085
knees first.

37
00:01:43,285 --> 00:01:46,415
Camels have thick, tough
skin on their knees,

38
00:01:46,455 --> 00:01:49,022
so they can kneel down on hot sand.

39
00:01:49,196 --> 00:01:51,966
Where do camels have tough, thick skin?

40
00:01:52,006 --> 00:01:54,359
On their knees, or on their ears?

41
00:01:57,679 --> 00:01:59,679
Tumble brings soft straw.

42
00:01:59,719 --> 00:02:02,389
Sandy kneels down, knees first.

43
00:02:02,429 --> 00:02:03,710
Ahh, just right!

44
00:02:04,058 --> 00:02:06,068
But now it is so quiet.

45
00:02:06,108 --> 00:02:08,710
At home, the desert wind goes whoosh.

46
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:09,710
I know!

47
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:12,460
Let's tiptoe outside,
and look at the stars!

48
00:02:12,647 --> 00:02:15,207
In the zoo garden, the moon is round and

49
00:02:15,247 --> 00:02:18,398
bright, and the sky is full of stars.

50
00:02:18,653 --> 00:02:20,683
How many big stars can you see?

51
00:02:20,723 --> 00:02:21,943
Count with me!

52
00:02:21,983 --> 00:02:24,367
One, two, three, four, five!

53
00:02:25,497 --> 00:02:26,147
Hush, hush!

54
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:28,366
Can you be very quiet, like the night?

55
00:02:29,486 --> 00:02:31,186
The stars are so pretty.

56
00:02:31,226 --> 00:02:33,085
But I am still wide awake.

57
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:35,178
Is it day, or night?

58
00:02:38,498 --> 00:02:41,718
Back in the barn, Sandy lies in the straw.

59
00:02:41,758 --> 00:02:43,398
Her eyes stay open.

60
00:02:43,646 --> 00:02:46,366
At home, Mama hums to me every night.

61
00:02:46,406 --> 00:02:48,059
I miss Mama's hum.

62
00:02:48,189 --> 00:02:51,459
Far away in the desert,
Mama camel looks up

63
00:02:51,499 --> 00:02:53,085
at the same big moon.

64
00:02:53,389 --> 00:02:56,523
Camel mamas and their
babies hum to each other!

65
00:02:56,908 --> 00:02:59,498
What do camel mamas and babies do?

66
00:02:59,538 --> 00:03:01,254
Hum, or roar?

67
00:03:04,574 --> 00:03:07,334
The barn is quiet and dark, and Mama is

68
00:03:07,374 --> 00:03:08,694
far away.

69
00:03:08,734 --> 00:03:10,585
Sandy feels a little sad.

70
00:03:10,927 --> 00:03:13,398
Maybe I am too little for a sleepover.

71
00:03:13,624 --> 00:03:14,674
Don't worry, Sandy.

72
00:03:14,714 --> 00:03:16,210
We are right here with you.

73
00:03:16,435 --> 00:03:19,155
Can good friends help Sandy feel better?

74
00:03:19,195 --> 00:03:20,703
Yes, or no?

75
00:03:24,063 --> 00:03:24,763
I know!

76
00:03:24,803 --> 00:03:26,843
I can teach you Mama's hum.

77
00:03:26,883 --> 00:03:29,023
Then a little bit of home is here with us!

78
00:03:29,338 --> 00:03:31,158
Yes! Teach us, Sandy!

79
00:03:31,198 --> 00:03:33,710
Tumble and Milo snuggle up close.

80
00:03:33,911 --> 00:03:36,281
Moon is round, stars are bright.

81
00:03:36,321 --> 00:03:38,398
Close your eyes, and sleep tight!

82
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:50,970
Her friends hum Mama's tune with her,

83
00:03:51,010 --> 00:03:52,730
soft and slow.

84
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:55,280
And Sandy falls fast asleep.

85
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:56,523
Sweet dreams!

86
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:58,933
What helped Sandy fall asleep?

87
00:03:58,973 --> 00:04:01,780
Mama's tune, or a loud drum?

88
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:05,880
Good morning!

89
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:07,240
The sun is up.

90
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,335
And look who is at the zoo gate!

91
00:04:09,588 --> 00:04:11,648
Mama! I slept all night!

92
00:04:11,688 --> 00:04:13,710
My friends hummed your tune with me.

93
00:04:13,847 --> 00:04:17,772
Mama camel and Sandy
hum hello, nose to nose.

94
00:04:18,023 --> 00:04:20,693
Then Mama and Sandy walk home together,

95
00:04:20,733 --> 00:04:22,439
side by side.

96
00:04:22,569 --> 00:04:24,269
Who was waiting at the gate?

97
00:04:24,309 --> 00:04:26,152
Mama, or Milo?

98
00:04:29,482 --> 00:04:31,835
Thank you for the sleepover, Sandy!

99
00:04:32,147 --> 00:04:32,987
Come again soon!

100
00:04:33,027 --> 00:04:34,960
Our barn is your barn too.

101
00:04:35,096 --> 00:04:36,486
Thank you, friends!

102
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:39,022
You made my first night away so cozy.

103
00:04:39,222 --> 00:04:41,682
When you miss someone,
a song from home can

104
00:04:41,722 --> 00:04:42,882
come with you.

105
00:04:42,922 --> 00:04:44,935
And good friends help, too.

106
00:04:45,075 --> 00:04:46,195
Do you remember?

107
00:04:46,235 --> 00:04:49,745
When can a baby camel
walk beside its mama?

108
00:04:49,785 --> 00:04:52,869
At half an hour old, or at one year old?

109
00:04:56,189 --> 00:04:58,539
And what keeps a camel's knees safe on hot

110
00:04:58,579 --> 00:05:02,362
sand? Tough skin, or soft feathers?

111
00:05:05,692 --> 00:05:08,212
Moon is round, stars are bright.

112
00:05:08,252 --> 00:05:10,585
Close your eyes, and sleep tight!

113
00:05:16,370 --> 00:05:19,890
Next time: Poppy's first slide on the ice!

114
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:22,460
See you on the next adventure, friends!

115
00:05:34,495 --> 00:05:36,282
The Animated Zoo!

